  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{1,2,3,4,5},{6,7}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{1,2,3,4,5},{6,7}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{1,2,3,4},{5},{6,7,8}}$ is not a partition because the element $8$ does not appear in $A.$\n\n- ${{1,2,3,4,5,6},{6,7}}$ is not a partition because the element $6$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{2,3,4,5,6,7}}$ is not a partition because the element $1\\in A$ does not appear in any subset.",
